<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh Dec 1996 oil output up 5.1 pct vs Nov.</title>
<headline>Kazakh Dec 1996 oil output up 5.1 pct vs Nov.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kazakhstan's production of crude oil and gas condensate rose to 2.14 million tonnes (equivalent to around 513,600 barrels per day) in December 1996 from 2.04 million (489,600 bpd) in November, the State Statistics Committee said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The committee provided the following figures:</p>
<p>  KAZAKH ENERGY OUTPUT	  DEC 96	 NOV 96     JAN-DEC 96</p>
<p>  Crude oil(million tonnes)   2.14	   2.04	  22.96</p>
<p>   mth/mth pct change	  +5.1	   +8.3	    n/a</p>
<p>   yr/yr   pct change	 +12.1	  +11.6	  +11.2</p>
<p>Natural gas</p>
<p>    (billion cubic metres)    0.66	   0.59	   6.4</p>
<p>   mth/mth pct change	 +11.3	  +15.3	    n/a</p>
<p>   yr/yr   pct change	  +2.3	   +5.0	   +8.1</p>
<p>  Gasoline (tonnes)	   143,000	168,500    2,274,800</p>
<p>   mth/mth pct change	 -15.1	  +49.4	    n/a</p>
<p>   yr/yr   pct change	 -36.3	  -22.44	  +4.4</p>
<p>  Diesel (tonnes)	     209,000	250,700    3,319,900</p>
<p>   mth/mth pct change	 -16.6	   +4.9	    n/a</p>
<p>   yr/yr   pct change	 -30.4	   -1.3	   +0.5</p>
<p>  Fuel oil (tonnes)	   325,200	324,300    3,758,200</p>
<p>   mth/mth pct change	  +0.3	   -3.5	    n/a</p>
<p>   yr/yr   pct change	 -15.9	  +37.6	   +3.9</p>
<p>NOTE - Comparative data for Jan-Dec 1995 was not available.</p>
<p>-- Almaty Newsroom +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
